    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **35 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors**, `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule on `POST /api/owners`, following the existing `DuplicateOwnerTelephoneException` convention already in the codebase:\n\n1. **New exception** \u2014 `DuplicateOwnerEmailException` (`rest/advice/`), carrying the offending email, mirroring the telephone/household duplicate exceptions.\n\n2. **Exception handler** \u2014 added `handleDuplicateOwnerEmailException` to `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, returning **409 Conflict** as a `ProblemDetail` with an `errors: [\"email\"]` property, matching the other duplicate handlers.\n\n3. **Controller check** \u2014 in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`, after the telephone-duplicate check, I compare the already-lower-cased `normalizedEmail` against every existing owner's email (case-insensitively) and throw the new exception when one matches. The check runs only when an email was supplied, since email is optional.\n\nThe rule correctly rejects the second owner sharing a lower-cased email with 409, and no existing behavior regressed.",
